  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1219 PM CDT Wed Oct 21 2026\n\nAn UL omega block has been established, with our CWA on the \neastern edge of the 250 mb ridge as of 16z. As such, high \nsurface pressure will be dominant until Monday at the earliest, \nleaving generally cloudless skies and seasonable, if not \nslightly above average, temperatures. Tuesday, long-range \nguidance suggests weak FROPA associated with the easterly \nprogression of the UL trough, but vorticity and frontogenesis \nvalues are low, and 250 mb flow is only weakly perturbed. GFS \nand ECMWF 500 mb relative humidity prog <40%, so chances of \nwidespread precipitation are minimal. A brief shower or two \ncannot be ruled out though, especially Tuesday morning in \nwestern parts of our coverage area.\n\nGiven weak surface flow, patchy areas of dense radiation fog \nare possible near bodies of water and in surrounding low-lying \nareas overnight through the morning. Widely scattered clouds \ntomorrow morning will not hinder the sun\u2019s ability to quickly \nerode this fog, so expect the fog threat to be eliminated by 15z\ntomorrow.",
